  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 335 AM CDT Fri Sep 11 2026\n\nThunderstorms are expected to develop over western Missouri on \nSaturday afternoon and evening and move eastward Saturday night. \nThere continues to be spread in the models on where these \nthunderstorms track, with the NAM showing a more robust complex of \nstorms that moves to the southeast that would affect central \nMissouri versus the GFS that has less QPF that moves to the east. We \nwill continue with just a 20-30% chance of showers and thunderstorms \nafter midnight on Saturday night.  There remains some possibility \nper the latest SWODY2 that one or two of these storms will be \ncapable of producing damaging winds along with locally heavy \nrainfall per WPC.\n\nThe chance for showers and thunderstorms will be mainly confined \nacross northeast Missouri and west central Illinois Sunday into \nMonday in close proximity to a front as a large upper high builds \nover the southern CONUS.  The front will move southeast by Tuesday \nand become stalled over the area through Thursday with the LREF \nhaving 40-60% of its members producing rain at St. Louis during this \ntimeframe.\n\nWith a front in the area, there will be a contrast in highs with 80s \nover the north and 90s in the south.",
